OctetRail is a Rust rewrite of dpkt, using dpkt as its Python API and behavior
reference. dpkt was created by Dug Song and maintained by its contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/kbandla/dpkt
Published reference: https://pypi.org/project/dpkt/1.9.8/

The Rust parser/writer, test harness and synthetic fixtures are original project work.
The Python facades adapt dpkt's capture iteration, callback methods, timestamp
rounding, UniversalReader selection, link-layer offset data and the covered
Ethernet field/packing behavior under its BSD license. dpkt's copyright and
license are retained in licenses/dpkt.txt.
Keep this notice and that license with source and binary distributions. No upstream endorsement is implied.

The fixed-header TCP API is compared with published dpkt 1.9.6 and 1.9.8.
The TCP core, facade, independent fixtures and tests are original project work;
dpkt remains the API/behavior reference under the retained BSD license.

CAPE is an external downstream smoke target, not the rewrite target. Its source
and tests are linked by revision, not redistributed here.

The IPv4 facade follows dpkt's fixed header fields and ordinary checksum
serialization behavior under the same retained upstream BSD license.

The fixed-header UDP API uses dpkt 1.9.6 and 1.9.8 as behavior references,
including retained length/checksum fields and opaque payload handling. The UDP
core, facade, independently constructed fixtures and tests are original work.
The applicable upstream BSD attribution and license above remain in force.
